      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017 The Authors. Published by Elsevier B.V. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "The human embryonic stem cell line NYSCFe003-A was derived from a day 5 to day 6 blastocyst in feeder-free and antibiotic free conditions. The blastocyst was voluntarily donated for research as surplus after in vitro fertilization treatment following informed consent. The NYSCFe003-A line expresses all the pluripotency markers and has the potential to differentiate into all three germ layers in vitro. The line presents normal karyotype and is mycoplasma free."
      },
